      "source_number": "873",
      "source_solution": "a) The natural numbers are 11 and 17. b) The unrestricted numbers have two unordered pairs: {10,12} and {-12,-10}; the source does not say natural or positive in b.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "domain": "Smaller number n is natural.",
          "derivation": "n(n+6)=187 gives n^2+6n-187=(n-11)(n+17)=0. n=-17 is not natural; 11*17=187 and 17-11=6.",
          "result": ["11", "17"],
          "units": "numbers"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "domain": "Smaller number u is real; no positivity requirement is stated.",
          "derivation": "u(u+2)=120 gives (u-10)(u+12)=0. u=10 yields (10,12); u=-12 yields (-12,-10). Both products are 120 and both ordered larger-minus-smaller differences are 2.",
          "result": [["10", "12"], ["-12", "-10"]],
          "units": "numbers"
        }
      ],
      "missing_source": []
    },
    {
